To make a particular user account usable only by WebSocket clients and not regular NATS connections, you would configure the user with the `allowed_connection_types` option in the `authorization` section of the configuration. Specifically, you would set the `allowed_connection_types` option to include `"WEBSOCKET"` and exclude any other types of connection types that should not be allowed for this user. Here is an example of how to set this up:

```json
authorization {
  users [
    {user: foo password: foopwd, permission: {...}, allowed_connection_types: ["WEBSOCKET"]}
    {user: bar password: barpwd, permission: {...}, allowed_connection_types: ["WEBSOCKET"]}
  ]
}
```

